er","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["api","c","lua","neovim","nvim","text-editor","vim"],"visibility":"public","forks":6465,"open_issues":2020,"watchers":94890,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"- `nvim --version`: NVIM v0.5.0-830-g4ae31c46f\r\n- `vim -u DEFAULTS` (version: ) behaves differently? yes (see below)\r\n- Operating system/version: Redhat 7.6\r\n- Terminal name/version: tmux 3.1\r\n- `$TERM`: tmux-256color\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce using `nvim -u NORC`\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ mkdir test; cd test\r\n$ for i in {1..300}; do mkdir -p $i; touch $i/$i.h; done\r\n$ cat << EOF > test.h\r\n#include \"99.h\"\r\nEOF\r\n$ cat << EOF > test.in\r\n:set path=\\$PWD/**\r\nWgf\r\nEOF\r\n$ nvim -u NORC test.h -s test.in\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Stack trace\r\n\r\n```\r\n(gdb) bt\r\n#0  0x00007f9e67c12207 in raise () from /usr/lib64/libc.so.6\r\n#1  0x00007f9e67c138f8 in abort () from /usr/lib64/libc.so.6\r\n#2  0x00007f9e67c0b026 in __assert_fail_base () from /usr/lib64/libc.so.6\r\n#3  0x00007f9e67c0b0d2 in __assert_fail () from /usr/lib64/libc.so.6\r\n#4  0x000000000055cc31 in vim_findfile (search_ctx_arg=0x228bf80) at ../src/nvim/file_search.c:853\r\n#5  0x000000000055de9b in find_file_in_path_option (ptr=0x20492c4 \"\", len=4, options=54, first=1, path_option=0x22e1fa0 \"/tmp/bug_test/**\", find_what=2, rel_fname=0x204ad80 \"/tmp/bug_test/test.h\", suffixes=0x2049020 \"\") at ../src/nvim/file_search.c:1513\r\n#6  0x000000000055da62 in find_file_in_path (ptr=0x22b94ba \"99.h\\\"\", len=4, options=54, first=1, rel_fname=0x204ad80 \"/tmp/bug_test/test.h\") at ../src/nvim/file_search.c:1349\r\n#7  0x000000000062b36e in find_file_name_in_path (ptr=0x22b94ba \"99.h\\\"\", len=4, options=55, count=1, rel_fname=0x204ad80 \"/tmp/bug_test/test.h\") at ../src/nvim/path.c:1649\r\n#8  0x00000000007248ed in file_name_in_line (line=0x22b94b0 \"#include \\\"99.h\\\"\", col=9, options=55, count=1, rel_fname=0x204ad80 \"/tmp/bug_test/test.h\", file_lnum=0x7ffe122793f8) at ../src/nvim/window.c:6196\r\n#9  0x000000000072449a in file_name_at_cursor (options=55, count=1, file_lnum=0x7ffe122793f8) at ../src/nvim/window.c:6078\r\n#10 0x000000000072442e in grab_file_name (count=1, file_lnum=0x7ffe122793f8) at ../src/nvim/window.c:6060\r\n#11 0x00000000005f4546 in nv_gotofile (cap=0x7ffe122795a8) at ../src/nvim/normal.c:5340\r\n#12 0x00000000005f83b1 in nv_g_cmd (cap=0x7ffe122795a8) at ../src/nvim/normal.c:6950\r\n#13 0x00000000005eae64 in normal_execute (state=0x7ffe12279520, key=103) at ../src/nvim/normal.c:1142\r\n#14 0x00000000006bc0ee in state_enter (s=0x7ffe12279520) at ../src/nvim/state.c:69\r\n#15 0x00000000005e915f in normal_enter (cmdwin=false, noexmode=false) at ../src/nvim/normal.c:463\r\n#16 0x00000000005a4b85 in main (argc=6, argv=0x7ffe122798a8) at ../src/nvim/main.c:557\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe problem appears to be that the `ffs_filearray_cur` member on the `ff_stack` is a `char_u` even though it's an index over an array that could have more than 255 members. vim does not have the assert on line 853 but is otherwise the same, and somehow it works there. I haven't dug in enough to know if the fact that the `ffs_filearray_cur` could overflow actually presents a problem in any practical sense, but it does seem wrong to my sensibilities.\r\n\r\nEither way, the problem can be fixed by changing that member to an int and updating the the assert accordingly. Doing so no longer crashes and works correctly.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/13284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/13284/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-r